* TR10 RX_VCO -- cross-coupled NMOS LC oscillator at 2*f_lo.
*
* The LO chain runs the VCO at 2*f_lo and divides by two, so the tank is at
* 2 MHz for a 1 MHz LO.  External LC: the tank is split into two halves from
* each drain to the AC-grounded centre node; the differential tank is
* L1+L2 = 15.9u*1e6/fc and C1 in series with C2.
*
*   Lh = Ltot/2, Ch = 1/(wc^2*Lh), Rh = Q*wc*Lh
*
* Cross-coupled pair: negative resistance -2/gm.  With a 1 mA tail the
* pair gives gm ~ 1.2 mS, i.e. -1.7 kohm against a 2 kohm differential tank,
* so start-up is comfortable.  Amplitude settles near I_tail*Rp = 2 V
* differential.
*
* vtune drives two NMOS varactors from each drain to the control node;
* the control node is bypassed, so the varactors appear in series across
* the tank.  The NMOS C-V saturates once Vgs > ~1 V, so the useful control
* range is 0..1 V around 0.5 V; the 0.97 factor on ch centres the free
* running frequency at 2 MHz there.
*
* Ports: out_p out_n vtune vdd vss
*   out_p/out_n  differential 2*f_lo, DC ~4 V, ~0.8 Vpp differential
*   vtune        0..5 V, centre ~2.5 V; see test_vco_tune.sp for the curve
*
* Symbolic values are for fc=2 MHz, Q=20.  rgval=1 on every analog MOS.
.subckt RX_VCO out_p out_n vtune vdd vss
.param fc=2e6 q=5 itail=1m
.param wc=2*3.141592653589793*fc
* Large L / small C keeps the tank capacitance comparable to the varactor:
* 15.9 uH per half at 2 MHz needs 398 pF per half, so the ~14 pF varactor
* gives a few percent of tuning range.
.param lh=15.9u
.param ch=0.8767/(wc*wc*lh)
.param rh=q*wc*lh

* ---- tank, split around the AC-grounded centre node --------------------
L1 out_p vct {lh}
L2 out_n vct {lh}
C1 out_p vss {ch}
C2 out_n vss {ch}
R1 out_p vct {rh}
R2 out_n vct {rh}
* centre node bias: drop ~1 V so the drains have upward swing room
* Bias the tank centre at 2.5 V: the source node then sits near 1 V and the
* body effect stays moderate.  Q=5 keeps Rp = 2 kohm differential so a 1 mA
* tail settles near 1 V per side instead of clipping.
Rfeed vdd vct 2.5k
Cct vct vss 10n

* ---- tuning varactors: gate = vtune, D/S/B = drain --------------------
XV1 vtune out_p NMOS_var w=9600u l=1u nf=16
XV2 vtune out_n NMOS_var w=9600u l=1u nf=16
Cv vtune vss 10n

* ---- cross-coupled pair -----------------------------------------------
X1 out_p out_n tail vss NMOS_nf w=200u l=1u nf=4 rgval=1
X2 out_n out_p tail vss NMOS_nf w=200u l=1u nf=4 rgval=1
Itail tail vss dc {itail}
.ends RX_VCO
